// Morph targets (blend shapes): a mesh that changes shape by a weighted sum
// of stored displacements, drawn by the ordinary pipelines, shadows
// included.
//
// glTF 2.0's MORPH TARGETS. A target is a displacement of the mesh's vertices
// (of its positions, and optionally of its normals and tangents); a morphed
// vertex is its base value plus the sum, over the targets, of the target's
// weight times the target's displacement; a morphed normal is made unit
// length again. The weights are ordinary numbers, not limited to 0 to 1, and
// the order is MORPH FIRST, THEN SKIN: the morphed vertex is what the bones
// carry. Unreal's morph targets, Unity's blend shapes, Godot's blend shapes
// and ARKit's face shapes are this model.
//
// METHOD: A COMPUTE PRE-PASS WRITING A COPY'S OWN VERTEX BUFFERS. Three
// ways to apply the sum are in use, and this is the second:
//   - in the vertex stage (Filament, Godot 3): every pipeline variant (lit,
//     physically based, blended, skinned, the eight shadow casters, the
//     velocity pass) grows morph code and a binding for the targets; the
//     vertex stage does the work again for every pass that draws the copy
//     (the main pass, each shadow cascade, each local light's faces);
//   - in a compute pre-pass writing the deformed vertices to buffers
//     (Unreal, Unity on desktop, Godot 4): the sum is done once a frame, a
//     draw reads positions and normals as for any mesh, and nothing else in
//     the renderer knows about morphing;
//   - transform feedback, which Vulkan does not have.
// The compute pre-pass costs memory (each morphed COPY has its own positions
// and normals, 24 bytes a vertex, and its own draw call: copies of one
// morphed mesh do not batch, since they differ in shape) and a dispatch for
// a copy whose weights changed; it saves the changes to every pipeline,
// makes skinning follow morphing for free (the skinned vertex stage reads
// the morphed buffers), makes every shadow caster cast the morphed shape,
// and a draw of a morphed copy costs what a draw of any mesh costs, however
// many targets the mesh has. A copy whose weights did not change since the
// last frame costs no compute at all.
//
// THE PARTS.
//   MorphTargets   the displacements, on the CPU: N targets over a mesh's M
//                  vertices, each target sparse (only the vertices it moves)
//                  or dense, positions, normals and tangents. It is
//                  gltfimport's morph target data in this package's own type
//                  (render does not import gltfimport); 'addDense' takes
//                  the three lists a glTF primitive's target holds. It also
//                  holds the CPU reference sum ('position', 'normal',
//                  'tangent') the GPU's is checked against.
//   Morpher        what runs the pre-pass: 'addSet' uploads a MorphTargets
//                  for a base mesh; 'addCopy' makes a morphed copy of a mesh
//                  the renderer holds, a MeshHandle of its own; 'setWeights'
//                  gives the copy its weights, the non-zero ones kept as a
//                  list sorted by target; 'update' records the compute pass
//                  for the copies whose weights changed. Call 'update' on the
//                  frame's encoder before 'Renderer.render'.
//   MorphMixer     the face-rig layer above the weights, CPU only: named
//                  channels (visemes, blinks) driving targets, with
//                  corrective targets that fire on a product of channels.
//
// A morphed copy's MeshHandle is used wherever a mesh's is: 'DrawList.add' or
// 'addSkinned' (if the base mesh is skinned, the copy has its joints and
// weights and takes its bones), the lit and physically based materials,
// blended or not, the sun's cascades and the local lights' shadows. Its
// bounding sphere is the base's grown by the sum, over the targets, of the
// weight's magnitude times the target's largest displacement, kept current by
// 'setWeights'. Remove a copy with 'removeCopy' here, not with
// 'removeMesh' (its compute work and bind group name its buffers).
//
// A COPY OWNS ALL ITS BUFFERS. A GPU buffer has one owner in this renderer
// (a GpuMesh holds its buffers, and a mesh's release destroys them), so a copy
// cannot borrow the base's index, uv, joint and weight buffers: 'addCopy'
// copies them on the GPU, once. That is the memory cost of this design for
// many copies of one mesh (a crowd of 100 faces of 10,000 vertices: about 60
// MB of vertex data in all); a base mesh may be replaced or removed once a
// copy exists. Sharing the unchanging streams between copies would be a change
// to GpuMesh (a reference-counted buffer), and is the first thing to do if a
// scene wants hundreds of morphing copies of one mesh.
//
// MEMORY AND LIMITS. A set holds per entry (a vertex a target moves) 4 bytes of
// target number and 24 of displacement, per vertex 4 of row pointer and 24 of
// the base mesh's positions and normals; a copy holds a mesh's buffers and 8
// bytes a target. 64 targets of 10,000 vertices, dense, is 18 MB; sparse, less.
// Any number of targets above 0 works (the active list holds as many as the
// set has targets); the largest set is the 128 MB a storage buffer binds
// (about 5 million entries). The tangent displacements glTF carries are kept
// in MorphTargets and used by its CPU reference but not uploaded: render has
// no tangent stream, finding tangents from screen-space derivatives.
//
// THE VELOCITY BUFFER. A temporal anti-aliasing pass wants each pixel's motion,
// including a morph's. 'addCopy' with 'keepPrevious' keeps the copy's
// positions of the frame before ('previousPositions'): a vertex buffer of the
// same layout as the copy's own, refreshed by 'update', so that a velocity
// pass can bind it as a second position stream and draw the difference of the
// two clip positions. It costs 12 more bytes a vertex and a buffer copy on a
// frame whose weights changed.
//
// A FACE RIG ON THIS. See MorphMixer: visemes and blinks are targets of the
// mesh, each modelled as a displacement from the neutral face; a viewer
// drives CHANNELS (jaw open, a viseme, blink left), each channel setting a
// weight of one or more targets (ARKit's 52 blend shapes are channels with
// one target each); targets are ADDITIVE, so a blink and a viseme sum; where
// two shapes together look wrong (a smile with the jaw wide open) a
// CORRECTIVE target, modelled as the difference between the true combined
// shape and the sum of the two, takes the product of the two channels as its
// weight, so it is on only as much as both are. Weights are computed on the
// CPU in the frame, from a keyframetracks clip's PROP_WEIGHTS track (or lip
// sync, or gaze), and handed to 'setWeights'.

// ---- The displacements ----

// How many bytes of the set's entry (six floats) and of an active pair (a
// target's number and weight)
const MORPH_ENTRY_BYTES = 24u64;
const MORPH_PAIR_BYTES = 8u64;

// The most vertices a workgroup of the compute shader covers
const MORPH_GROUP_SIZE = 64u32;

// A mesh's morph targets on the CPU: N targets, each the vertices it moves
// and by how much. Entries are kept in the order of the targets, vertices
// ascending within a target.
pub struct MorphTargets {
  pub vertexCount: usize;            // the mesh's vertices: every target is over these
  pub targetStart: List[u32];        // N + 1 entries: target t's entries are targetStart[t] to targetStart[t + 1] - 1
  pub vertex: List[u32];             // each entry's vertex
  pub dPos: List[Vec3];              // and its displacement of the position,
  pub dNor: List[Vec3];              // of the normal
  pub dTan: List[Vec3];              // and of the tangent's xyz
  pub maxMove: List[f32];            // each target's largest position displacement

  // No targets, over a mesh of 'vertexCount' vertices
  pub fn empty(vertexCount: usize) MorphTargets {
    var starts = List[u32].empty();
    starts.push(0u32);
    new MorphTargets(vertexCount, starts, List[u32].empty(), List[Vec3].empty(), List[Vec3].empty(),
      List[Vec3].empty(), List[f32].empty())
  }

  // How many targets
  pub fn count(self: &) usize { targetStart.len() - 1usize }

  // How many entries in all
  pub fn entryCount(self: &) usize { vertex.len() }

  // How many vertices target 't' moves
  pub fn targetEntries(self: &, t: usize) usize { usize.from(*targetStart[t + 1usize] - *targetStart[t]) }

  // Add a target from lists with one displacement a vertex (the lists of
  // gltfimport's MorphTarget): 'positions', 'normals' and 'tangents', any of
  // which may be empty (no displacement of that). A vertex all three leave
  // exactly where they were is not stored. A list of any other length than
  // the mesh's vertices is taken as empty. Answers the target's number.
  pub fn addDense(self: &mut, positions: &List[Vec3], normals: &List[Vec3], tangents: &List[Vec3]) usize {
    let n = vertexCount;
    let hasP = positions.len() == n;
    let hasN = normals.len() == n;
    let hasT = tangents.len() == n;
    let zero = new Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
    var biggest: f32 = 0.;
    var v = 0usize;
    while v < n {
      let p = if hasP { *positions[v] } else { zero };
      let nm = if hasN { *normals[v] } else { zero };
      let tg = if hasT { *tangents[v] } else { zero };
      if p.x != 0. || p.y != 0. || p.z != 0. || nm.x != 0. || nm.y != 0. || nm.z != 0.
          || tg.x != 0. || tg.y != 0. || tg.z != 0. {
        vertex.push(u32.from(v));
        dPos.push(p);
        dNor.push(nm);
        dTan.push(tg);
        let len = p.length();
        if len > biggest { biggest = len; }
      }
      v = v + 1usize;
    }
    maxMove.push(biggest);
    targetStart.push(u32.from(vertex.len()));
    targetStart.len() - 2usize
  }

  // Add a target from glTF's sparse form: the displacements of the vertices
  // in 'indices' only, 'positions', 'normals' and 'tangents' one for each
  // index (or empty). An index past the mesh is ignored; one given twice
  // keeps the last. Answers the target's number.
  pub fn addSparse(self: &mut, indices: &List[u32], positions: &List[Vec3], normals: &List[Vec3],
      tangents: &List[Vec3]) usize {
    let zero = new Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
    var dp = List[Vec3].empty();
    var dn = List[Vec3].empty();
    var dt = List[Vec3].empty();
    var v = 0usize;
    while v < vertexCount {
      dp.push(zero);
      dn.push(zero);
      dt.push(zero);
      v = v + 1usize;
    }
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < indices.len() {
      let at = usize.from(*indices[i]);
      if at < vertexCount {
        if positions.len() == indices.len() { dp.set(at, *positions[i]); }
        if normals.len() == indices.len() { dn.set(at, *normals[i]); }
        if tangents.len() == indices.len() { dt.set(at, *tangents[i]); }
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    self.addDense(&dp, &dn, &dt)
  }

  // The position of vertex 'v', modelled at 'base', morphed by 'weights' (one
  // a target; a target past the end of the list has weight 0): the CPU's twin
  // of morph.slang, summing in the same order (the targets ascending, a
  // target of weight 0 left out)
  pub fn position(self: &, v: usize, base: Vec3, weights: &List[f32]) Vec3 {
    var p = base;
    var t = 0usize;
    while t < self.count() && t < weights.len() {
      let w = *weights[t];
      if w != 0. {
        let e = self.find(t, v);
        if e >= 0i64 { p = p + *dPos[usize.from(e)] * w; }
      }
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    p
  }

  // The normal of vertex 'v', modelled at 'base': morphed, then made unit
  // length (left as it was if no weight reaches the vertex)
  pub fn normal(self: &, v: usize, base: Vec3, weights: &List[f32]) Vec3 {
    var n = base;
    var touched = false;
    var t = 0usize;
    while t < self.count() && t < weights.len() {
      let w = *weights[t];
      if w != 0. {
        let e = self.find(t, v);
        if e >= 0i64 {
          n = n + *dNor[usize.from(e)] * w;
          touched = true;
        }
      }
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    if touched && n.length() > 1.0e-12 { n = n.normalize(); }
    n
  }

  // The tangent's xyz of vertex 'v', modelled at 'base', morphed (glTF: the
  // handedness is not morphed, and the result is not made unit length)
  pub fn tangent(self: &, v: usize, base: Vec3, weights: &List[f32]) Vec3 {
    var g = base;
    var t = 0usize;
    while t < self.count() && t < weights.len() {
      let w = *weights[t];
      if w != 0. {
        let e = self.find(t, v);
        if e >= 0i64 { g = g + *dTan[usize.from(e)] * w; }
      }
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    g
  }

  // The entry of target 't' for vertex 'v', or -1: a binary search of the
  // target's entries, which ascend by vertex
  pub fn find(self: &, t: usize, v: usize) i64 {
    var lo = usize.from(*targetStart[t]);
    var hi = usize.from(*targetStart[t + 1usize]);
    let want = u32.from(v);
    while lo < hi {
      let mid = (lo + hi) / 2usize;
      if *vertex[mid] < want { lo = mid + 1usize; } else { hi = mid; }
    }
    if lo < usize.from(*targetStart[t + 1usize]) && *vertex[lo] == want { return i64.from(lo); }
    -1i64
  }
}

// ---- The GPU's side ----

// A set of targets uploaded for a base mesh (the compressed per-vertex rows
// morph.slang reads)
pub struct MorphSetSlot {
  rowStart: Buffer;
  entryTarget: Buffer;
  entryDelta: Buffer;
  basePosition: Buffer;
  baseNormal: Buffer;
  vertexCount: u32;
  targetCount: u32;
  maxMove: List[f32];         // each target's largest position displacement
}

// A morphed copy: its mesh in the renderer and what it is built from
pub struct MorphCopySlot {
  set: Ref[MorphSetSlot];
  mesh: MeshHandle;
  previous: Buffer;           // last frame's positions, if asked for; else none
  active: Buffer;             // the active list: (target, weight) pairs, 8 bytes each
  group: BindGroup;
  weights: List[f32];         // one a target, as last set
  pairs: List[f32];           // the active list on the CPU: target (as the bits of a u32) and weight
  activeCount: u32;
  baseRadius: f32;
  dirty: bool;                // the weights changed since the last update
  previousStale: bool;        // 'previous' is not yet the frame the positions now are
}

// A set of targets the Morpher holds
pub struct MorphSetHandle {
  pub slot: Ref[MorphSetSlot];

  pub fn none() MorphSetHandle { new MorphSetHandle(Ref[MorphSetSlot].none()) }
  pub fn isNone(self) bool { slot.isNone() }
}

// A morphed copy the Morpher holds
pub struct MorphHandle {
  pub slot: Ref[MorphCopySlot];

  pub fn none() MorphHandle { new MorphHandle(Ref[MorphCopySlot].none()) }
  pub fn isNone(self) bool { slot.isNone() }
}

// What runs the morph pre-pass. Make one with 'create' and check 'isValid'.
pub struct Morpher {
  shader: ShaderModule;
  groupLayout: BindGroupLayout;
  layout: PipelineLayout;
  pipeline: ComputePipeline;
  sets: Pool[MorphSetSlot];
  copies: Pool[MorphCopySlot];
  order: List[MorphHandle];         // the live copies, in the order they were made
  pub dispatches: u32 = 0u32;       // how many copies the last 'update' recomputed

  pub fn create(device: &mut Device) Morpher {
    let readOnly = BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_READ_ONLY_STORAGE;
    let entries = [
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 0u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: readOnly),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 1u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: readOnly),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 2u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: readOnly),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 3u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: readOnly),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 4u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: readOnly),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 5u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: readOnly),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 6u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_STORAGE),
      new BindGroupLayoutEntry(binding: 7u32, visibility: SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE, bufferType: BUFFER_BINDING_TYPE_STORAGE)];
    var groupLayout = device.createBindGroupLayout(&entries);
    let groupLayouts = [&groupLayout];
    var layout = device.createPipelineLayout(&groupLayouts, 12u32);
    var shader = device.createShaderModule(&MORPH_SPIRV);
    let desc = new ComputePipelineDescriptor(layout: &layout, module: &shader, entryPoint: "morphMain");
    var pipeline = device.createComputePipeline(&desc);
    new Morpher(shader, groupLayout, layout, pipeline, Pool[MorphSetSlot].empty(), Pool[MorphCopySlot].empty(), List[MorphHandle].empty(), 0u32)
  }

  pub fn isValid(self: &) bool { pipeline.isValid() }

  // Upload 'targets' for copies of 'base', the mesh they are targets of (the
  // vertices the renderer's own copy of it has, in its order). Normals the
  // mesh lacks are made smooth, as the renderer makes them. None if the
  // vertex counts differ or the mesh has no vertices.
  pub fn addSet(self: &mut, device: &mut Device, targets: &MorphTargets, base: &Mesh) MorphSetHandle {
    let n = base.positions.len();
    if n == 0usize || n != targets.vertexCount { return MorphSetHandle.none(); }
    var withNormals = Mesh.empty();
    withNormals.append(base);
    if withNormals.normals.len() != n { withNormals.computeSmoothNormals(); }
    let storage = BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_SRC;
    let entries = targets.entryCount();
    // The rows: for each vertex, the entries of every target that moves it,
    // by target. Counted, then filled in target order, which leaves each row
    // ascending by target.
    var counts = List[u32].empty();
    var v = 0usize;
    while v <= n {
      counts.push(0u32);
      v = v + 1usize;
    }
    var e = 0usize;
    while e < entries {
      let at = usize.from(*targets.vertex[e]);
      counts.set(at + 1usize, *counts[at + 1usize] + 1u32);
      e = e + 1usize;
    }
    var rows = List[u32].empty();
    var run = 0u32;
    v = 0usize;
    while v <= n {
      run = run + *counts[v];
      rows.push(run);
      v = v + 1usize;
    }
    var fill = List[u32].empty();
    v = 0usize;
    while v < n {
      fill.push(*rows[v]);
      v = v + 1usize;
    }
    var targetOf = List[u32].empty();
    var deltas = List[f32].empty();
    e = 0usize;
    while e < entries {
      targetOf.push(0u32);
      v = 0usize;
      while v < 6usize {
        deltas.push(0.);
        v = v + 1usize;
      }
      e = e + 1usize;
    }
    var t = 0usize;
    while t < targets.count() {
      var k = usize.from(*targets.targetStart[t]);
      let end = usize.from(*targets.targetStart[t + 1usize]);
      while k < end {
        let at = usize.from(*targets.vertex[k]);
        let slot = usize.from(*fill[at]);
        fill.set(at, *fill[at] + 1u32);
        targetOf.set(slot, u32.from(t));
        let p = *targets.dPos[k];
        let nm = *targets.dNor[k];
        deltas.set(slot * 6usize, p.x);
        deltas.set(slot * 6usize + 1usize, p.y);
        deltas.set(slot * 6usize + 2usize, p.z);
        deltas.set(slot * 6usize + 3usize, nm.x);
        deltas.set(slot * 6usize + 4usize, nm.y);
        deltas.set(slot * 6usize + 5usize, nm.z);
        k = k + 1usize;
      }
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    var slot = new MorphSetSlot(
      uploadWords(device, bytesOf[u32](&rows), u64.from(n + 1usize) * 4u64, storage),
      uploadWords(device, if entries > 0usize { bytesOf[u32](&targetOf) } else { 0usize as *u8 }, u64.from(entries) * 4u64, storage),
      uploadWords(device, if entries > 0usize { bytesOf[f32](&deltas) } else { 0usize as *u8 }, u64.from(entries) * MORPH_ENTRY_BYTES, storage),
      uploadWords(device, bytesOf[Vec3](&withNormals.positions), u64.from(n) * 12u64, storage),
      uploadWords(device, bytesOf[Vec3](&withNormals.normals), u64.from(n) * 12u64, storage),
      u32.from(n), u32.from(targets.count()), List[f32].empty());
    t = 0usize;
    while t < targets.count() {
      slot.maxMove.push(*targets.maxMove[t]);
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    new MorphSetHandle(sets.add(slot))
  }

  // Take the set 'h' away (its buffers are released when the GPU is done
  // with them). Copies made from it must be removed first.
  pub fn removeSet(self: &mut, device: &mut Device, h: MorphSetHandle) bool {
    if !sets.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    {
      var s = &mut sets[h.slot];
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut s.rowStart);
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut s.entryTarget);
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut s.entryDelta);
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut s.basePosition);
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut s.baseNormal);
    }
    sets.remove(h.slot)
  }

  // A morphed copy of the mesh 'base' (which the renderer holds, uploaded
  // from the Mesh 'set' was made for), all weights 0: a mesh of the renderer's
  // of its own, drawn as any is, as modelled until 'setWeights' says
  // otherwise. The copying of the base's streams is recorded into
  // 'encoder', which must be submitted before the copy is drawn (a frame's
  // own, ahead of 'update', does: many copies made in one frame share it).
  // 'keepPrevious' keeps last frame's positions ('previousPositions'). None
  // if either handle names nothing, the base has other than the set's vertex
  // count, or it is lines.
  pub fn addCopy(self: &mut, device: &mut Device, encoder: &mut CommandEncoder, renderer: &mut Renderer,
      base: MeshHandle, set: MorphSetHandle, keepPrevious: bool) MorphHandle {
    if !renderer.meshes.alive(base.slot) || !sets.alive(set.slot) { return MorphHandle.none(); }
    let count = sets[set.slot].vertexCount;
    let vertexUsage = BUFFER_USAGE_VERTEX | BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_SRC;
    var g = GpuMesh.none();
    {
      let b = renderer.meshes[base.slot].current();
      if b.vertexCount != count || b.topology != PRIMITIVE_TOPOLOGY_TRIANGLE_LIST || !b.isValid() {
        return MorphHandle.none();
      }
      // The streams the weights do not change are copied, on the GPU: a
      // buffer has one owner, so a mesh cannot borrow another's
      g.uvs = cloneBuffer(device, encoder, &b.uvs);
      g.indices = cloneBuffer(device, encoder, &b.indices);
      g.joints = cloneBuffer(device, encoder, &b.joints);
      g.weights = cloneBuffer(device, encoder, &b.weights);
      g.sway = cloneBuffer(device, encoder, &b.sway);
      g.vertexCount = b.vertexCount;
      g.indexCount = b.indexCount;
      g.topology = b.topology;
      g.center = b.center;
      g.radius = b.radius;
      var i = 0usize;
      while i < b.groups.len() {
        g.groups.push(*b.groups[i]);
        i = i + 1usize;
      }
    }
    let bytes = u64.from(count) * 12u64;
    g.positions = device.createBuffer(bytes, vertexUsage);
    g.normals = device.createBuffer(bytes, vertexUsage);
    // As modelled, until the first weights come: the set's copy of the base
    encoder.copyBufferToBuffer(&sets[set.slot].basePosition, 0u64, &g.positions, 0u64, bytes);
    encoder.copyBufferToBuffer(&sets[set.slot].baseNormal, 0u64, &g.normals, 0u64, bytes);
    var previous = Buffer.none();
    if keepPrevious {
      previous = device.createBuffer(bytes, vertexUsage);
      encoder.copyBufferToBuffer(&sets[set.slot].basePosition, 0u64, &previous, 0u64, bytes);
    }
    let targetCount = sets[set.slot].targetCount;
    var active = device.createBuffer(max64(u64.from(targetCount) * MORPH_PAIR_BYTES, 16u64),
      BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST);
    let groupEntries = [
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(0u32, &sets[set.slot].rowStart),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(1u32, &sets[set.slot].entryTarget),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(2u32, &sets[set.slot].entryDelta),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(3u32, &sets[set.slot].basePosition),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(4u32, &sets[set.slot].baseNormal),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(5u32, &active),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(6u32, &g.positions),
      BindGroupEntry.buffer(7u32, &g.normals)];
    var group = device.createBindGroup(&self.groupLayout, &groupEntries);
    var weights = List[f32].empty();
    var t = 0u32;
    while t < targetCount {
      weights.push(0.);
      t = t + 1u32;
    }
    let copy = new MorphCopySlot(set.slot, MeshHandle.none(), previous, active, group, weights,
      List[f32].empty(), 0u32, g.radius, false, false);
    let mesh = new MeshHandle(renderer.meshes.add(new MeshSlot(g, GpuMesh.none(), 0u32, false, 0u64, 0u32)));
    var h = new MorphHandle(copies.add(copy));
    copies[h.slot].mesh = mesh;
    self.order.push(h);
    h
  }

  // Take the copy 'h' away: its mesh leaves the renderer and its buffers are
  // released, the base's shared ones left alone
  pub fn removeCopy(self: &mut, device: &mut Device, renderer: &mut Renderer, h: MorphHandle) bool {
    if !copies.alive(h.slot) { return false; }
    {
      var c = &mut copies[h.slot];
      if renderer.meshes.alive(c.mesh.slot) { renderer.removeMesh(device, c.mesh); }
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut c.previous);
      device.queue.releaseBuffer(&mut c.active);
    }
    var kept = List[MorphHandle].empty();
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < self.order.len() {
      if !(self.order[i].slot == h.slot) { kept.push(*self.order[i]); }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    self.order = kept;
    copies.remove(h.slot)
  }

  // The mesh the copy 'h' is drawn as (none if 'h' names no copy)
  pub fn mesh(self: &, h: MorphHandle) MeshHandle {
    if !copies.alive(h.slot) { return MeshHandle.none(); }
    copies[h.slot].mesh
  }

  // The copy's positions of the frame before, for a velocity pass: valid
  // after the copy was made with 'keepPrevious' (the buffer is not valid
  // otherwise), and current as of the last 'update'
  pub fn previousPositions(self: &, h: MorphHandle) &Buffer {
    &copies[h.slot].previous
  }

  // How many targets the copy has weights for
  pub fn targetCount(self: &, h: MorphHandle) usize {
    if !copies.alive(h.slot) { return 0usize; }
    copies[h.slot].weights.len()
  }

  // The copy's weights as last set
  pub fn weights(self: &, h: MorphHandle, out: &mut List[f32]) {
    out.clear();
    if !copies.alive(h.slot) { return; }
    let c = copies[h.slot];
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < c.weights.len() {
      out.push(*c.weights[i]);
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // How many targets are not zero now (the active list's length)
  pub fn activeCount(self: &, h: MorphHandle) u32 {
    if !copies.alive(h.slot) { return 0u32; }
    copies[h.slot].activeCount
  }

  // Give the copy 'h' its weights, one a target (a missing weight is 0, an
  // extra one is ignored). The ones that are not zero make the active list,
  // sorted by target; if no weight differs from the last call's, nothing is
  // marked to be done. The copy's bounding sphere is made to hold the shape
  // the weights give.
  pub fn setWeights(self: &mut, renderer: &mut Renderer, h: MorphHandle, weights: &List[f32]) {
    if !copies.alive(h.slot) { return; }
    var c = &mut copies[h.slot];
    let set = sets[c.set];
    var changed = false;
    var t = 0usize;
    while t < c.weights.len() {
      let w = if t < weights.len() { *weights[t] } else { 0. };
      if w != *c.weights[t] {
        c.weights.set(t, w);
        changed = true;
      }
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    if !changed { return; }
    c.pairs.clear();
    c.activeCount = 0u32;
    var grow: f32 = 0.;
    t = 0usize;
    while t < c.weights.len() {
      let w = *c.weights[t];
      if w != 0. {
        c.pairs.push(u32.from(t) as f32);
        c.pairs.push(w);
        c.activeCount = c.activeCount + 1u32;
        grow = grow + (if w < 0. { -w } else { w }) * *set.maxMove[t];
      }
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    c.dirty = true;
    if renderer.meshes.alive(c.mesh.slot) { renderer.meshes[c.mesh.slot].a.radius = c.baseRadius + grow; }
  }

  // Record the pre-pass for every copy whose weights changed since the last
  // call into 'encoder', before the render that draws them. A copy kept
  // 'keepPrevious' first has its positions copied to 'previous'. Answers how
  // many copies were recomputed (also 'dispatches').
  pub fn update(self: &mut, device: &mut Device, encoder: &mut CommandEncoder, renderer: &Renderer) u32 {
    var count = 0u32;
    // The frame before's positions, copied outside the compute pass
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < self.order.len() {
      var c = &mut copies[self.order[i].slot];
      if c.previous.isValid() {
        let bytes = u64.from(sets[c.set].vertexCount) * 12u64;
        let positions = &renderer.meshes[c.mesh.slot].current().positions;
        if c.dirty {
          encoder.copyBufferToBuffer(positions, 0u64, &c.previous, 0u64, bytes);
          c.previousStale = true;
        } elif c.previousStale {
          encoder.copyBufferToBuffer(positions, 0u64, &c.previous, 0u64, bytes);
          c.previousStale = false;
        }
      }
      if c.dirty { count = count + 1u32; }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    if count > 0u32 {
      var pass = encoder.beginComputePass();
      pass.setPipeline(&self.pipeline);
      i = 0usize;
      while i < self.order.len() {
        var c = &mut copies[self.order[i].slot];
        if c.dirty {
          if c.activeCount > 0u32 {
            device.queue.writeBuffer(&c.active, 0u64, bytesOf[f32](&c.pairs), u64.from(c.activeCount) * MORPH_PAIR_BYTES);
          }
          pass.setBindGroup(0u32, &c.group);
          let immediates: Array[u32, 3] = [sets[c.set].vertexCount, c.activeCount, sets[c.set].targetCount];
          pass.setImmediates(0u32, &immediates as *u8, 12u32);
          pass.dispatchWorkgroups((sets[c.set].vertexCount + MORPH_GROUP_SIZE - 1u32) / MORPH_GROUP_SIZE);
          c.dirty = false;
        }
        i = i + 1usize;
      }
      pass.end();
    }
    self.dispatches = count;
    count
  }
}

// A buffer holding what 'source' holds, copied by the GPU through 'encoder'
// (none, if 'source' is none)
fn cloneBuffer(device: &mut Device, encoder: &mut CommandEncoder, source: &Buffer) Buffer {
  if !source.isValid() { return Buffer.none(); }
  var b = device.createBuffer(source.size, source.usage | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_DST | BUFFER_USAGE_COPY_SRC);
  encoder.copyBufferToBuffer(source, 0u64, &b, 0u64, source.size);
  b
}

// Bytes to the GPU: a buffer of at least 16 bytes holding 'size' bytes from 'data'
fn uploadWords(device: &mut Device, data: *u8, size: u64, usage: u32) Buffer {
  var b = device.createBuffer(max64(size, 16u64), usage);
  if size > 0u64 && (data as usize) != 0usize { device.queue.writeBuffer(&b, 0u64, data, size); }
  b
}

fn max64(a: u64, b: u64) u64 { if a > b { a } else { b } }

// ---- A face rig's weights ----

// The layer between a face's controls and the targets' weights, on the CPU.
// A CHANNEL is a control a program or an animation sets, 0 to 1 as a rule
// (jaw open, a viseme, blink left, a smile); it DRIVES one or more targets,
// each at a scale (a smile channel drives the smile target at 1 and the
// cheek target at 0.5; a negative scale lets one channel ease another's
// target back). Contributions ADD, so a viseme and a blink sum without
// either knowing of the other. A CORRECTIVE target is for the pose two
// channels make together that the sum of their targets gets wrong (a wide
// smile with the jaw open pulls the lip through the teeth): it is modelled
// as the difference between the true combined shape and the sum of the two,
// and its weight is the PRODUCT of the two channels' values, so it is
// fully on only when both are, and not at all when either is off. This is
// the combination-shape rule of Maya and Blender's shape keys, and of
// ARKit's face rigs.
//
// 'resolve' makes the weights for a mesh's targets, to hand to
// 'Morpher.setWeights'. Nothing is clamped unless 'clampTo' says (glTF
// allows weights outside 0 to 1, for exaggeration).
pub struct MorphMixer {
  pub targetCount: usize;
  values: List[f32];              // each channel's value
  driveChannel: List[u32];        // the drives: a channel, a target, a scale
  driveTarget: List[u32];
  driveScale: List[f32];
  corrA: List[u32];               // the correctives: two channels and a target
  corrB: List[u32];
  corrTarget: List[u32];
  clamped: bool;
  lo: f32;
  hi: f32;

  pub fn make(targetCount: usize) MorphMixer {
    new MorphMixer(targetCount, List[f32].empty(), List[u32].empty(), List[u32].empty(), List[f32].empty(),
      List[u32].empty(), List[u32].empty(), List[u32].empty(), false, 0., 1.)
  }

  // A new channel, at 0; its number
  pub fn addChannel(self: &mut) usize {
    values.push(0.);
    values.len() - 1usize
  }

  // Channel 'channel' adds its value times 'scale' to target 'target'
  pub fn drive(self: &mut, channel: usize, target: usize, scale: f32) {
    driveChannel.push(u32.from(channel));
    driveTarget.push(u32.from(target));
    driveScale.push(scale);
  }

  // Target 'target' is the corrective of channels 'a' and 'b': its weight is
  // their values' product
  pub fn corrective(self: &mut, a: usize, b: usize, target: usize) {
    corrA.push(u32.from(a));
    corrB.push(u32.from(b));
    corrTarget.push(u32.from(target));
  }

  // Channel 'channel' takes 'value'
  pub fn set(self: &mut, channel: usize, value: f32) {
    if channel < values.len() { values.set(channel, value); }
  }

  // The weights end up between 'low' and 'high'
  pub fn clampTo(self: &mut, low: f32, high: f32) {
    clamped = true;
    lo = low;
    hi = high;
  }

  // The weight of every target from the channels now, into 'out'
  pub fn resolve(self: &, out: &mut List[f32]) {
    out.clear();
    var t = 0usize;
    while t < targetCount {
      out.push(0.);
      t = t + 1usize;
    }
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < driveChannel.len() {
      let target = usize.from(*driveTarget[i]);
      let channel = usize.from(*driveChannel[i]);
      if target < targetCount && channel < values.len() {
        out.set(target, *out[target] + *values[channel] * *driveScale[i]);
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    i = 0usize;
    while i < corrTarget.len() {
      let target = usize.from(*corrTarget[i]);
      let a = usize.from(*corrA[i]);
      let b = usize.from(*corrB[i]);
      if target < targetCount && a < values.len() && b < values.len() {
        out.set(target, *out[target] + *values[a] * *values[b]);
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    if clamped {
      t = 0usize;
      while t < targetCount {
        let w = *out[t];
        out.set(t, if w < lo { lo } elif w > hi { hi } else { w });
        t = t + 1usize;
      }
    }
  }
}

